    {
        "id": "54480b212d570649",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "1b38d77dcadc045b",
        "name": "READ ME",
        "info": "4/6/29 - Update\nDisabling nightly runs for now. Functionality can still be run by manually injecting. The\n'repeat' injection has been disconnected.\n\nThis flow operates by interfacing with the API of the Security app. An existing scan job \nis run at 11:59 pm every night. When the job completes, the zipped report is downloaded\nand decompressed. The PDF report is saved to the micro SD card under the 'SecurityReports'\ndirectory as 'DailySecurityReport.pdf' and sent to the email address set in the \n'Define Email Properties' node. Finally the report is deleted from the Security Scanner\nApp memory to conserve space.\n\nExamples use palette 'node-red-node-email' for email node and 'node-red-contrib-zip' for\nfile decompression.",
        "x": 100,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
